{"title":"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A bamboo plant grows at a rate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791f15f656db201fa9116a2f762a4b292fc50883.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$105$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> cm per day. On May 1st at noon it was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/9/09930426d38eccb974422733e80ed818dcb14f2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 m$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" /> tall.  Approximately how tall, in metres, was it on May 8th at noon?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/2/292344a6a3eb10eff7132f206625f441c6d7834e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 10.40 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 8.30 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 3.05 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 7.35 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 9.35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"455\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the bamboo plant grows at a rate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/1/c31f127c6f44a7a091da9fd18842b792afac7492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$105 cm$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" /> per day and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> days separating May 1st and May 8th, then it grows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/0/3d029c797dd9e0fb98671ae89f6ab82d53fa3d6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7\\times 105 = 735 cm$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"133\" height=\"13\" /> in this time period.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/d/f6de552b38b2953c84be7c05763f1e0e702a5211.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$735 cm = 7.35 m$\" width=\"123\" height=\"12\" />, then the height of the plant on May 8th is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b643686db2920db2cf35b3b86307c78b1492d507.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 7.35 = 9.35 m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"135\" height=\"14\" />.  The correct answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\